ity and Partners Find Us Contact Us Faculty/Staff Directory Maps & Directions Image Logins Image Academic Calendar Image Locations FIND IT Visit Apply Now Request Information Virtual Tour Logins Results See All About Directory Student Experience Athletics Maps Jobs at AU Programs Book Store Financial Aid & Tuition Make a Gift Recent News Sep 1, 2026 Alvernia University forms alliance with Independence Blue Cross to Expand Educational Opportunities The new relationship creates flexible, affordable pathways for Independence Blue Cross associates to earn undergraduate and graduate degrees while advancing their careers Alvernia University has joined … Aug 26, 2026 Alvernia’s Electrical and Mechanical Engineering Programs Receive ABET Accreditation Accreditation affirms that the university’s programs meet the quality standards established by the engineering professionAlvernia University’s Bachelor of Science programs in electrical engineering and mechanical… Aug 24, 2026 Alvernia President Fitzgerald featured in article about workplace adaptability Alvernia President Glynis A. Fitzgerald, Ph.D., was featured in \"Adaptability in the Workplace,\" an article written by Adam Mendler, a nationally recognized authority on leadership.\"Adaptability in the workplace is becoming… See All News Upcoming Events Data Analytics Virtual Information Session Achieve More With A Data Analytics… Thursday, Sep 10, 6:00 pm - 7:00 pm DPT Virtual Information Session Thursday, Sep 17, 6:00 pm - 7:00 pm Latinos Unidos: A Hispanic Heritage Month Celebration Register Here Theme: ¡Unidos, Somos Más! (Together, We Are One!)Location: Alvernia University, Francis Hall Atrium and Theatre, 400 Saint Bernardine Street, Reading, PA… Friday, Sep 25, 5:00 pm - 8:30 pm FAQs What type of financial aid is available? At Alvernia, applying for financial aid is easy. We encourage all prospective Alvernia students to apply, even if you feel you may not be eligible for assistance. The Office of Student Financial Services is available to answer questions and guide you through any financial aid situation, email us, call us at 610-796-8201 or stop by the office in Room 114 of Bernardine Hall. Read more financial aid, fees, FAFSA, and billing FAQs How do I Create My Comeback? At Alvernia, we’re in the business of supporting and affirming people in the pursuit of changing their lives for good. If the vision you have of your life includes making an impact on the world, up-leveling your career growth, building a better life for your family, serving your community, or becoming the leader you’ve always known yourself to be - join us to kick-start your next steps. You’re here to get ahead, we're here to help. Contact our knowledgeable admissions coordinators for more information at gradandadult@alvernia.edu , 610-796-5187 When will I receive housing information if I am an incoming first-year or transfer student? The Office of Residence Life will begin to communicate with incoming first-year and transfer students with complete detailed instructions by the end of February.  Our goal is to open the incoming student housing application no later than mid-March. When should I apply? The path to college is a process that typically starts in high school. Our Undergraduate Admissions Office is devoted to helping students and their families through this important and exciting time by arranging visits, hosting events, and answering questions to help you meet future goals and craft a fulfilling life. And, we want you to experience the many ways that Alvernia can help you do this! INQUIRE GIVE VISIT APPLY Breadcrumb Home Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Admissions Admitted Students Confirm Your Enrollment Error message Confirm Your Enrollment Confirm Your Enrollment Congratulations on your acceptance to Alvernia University! At Alvernia, we offer three convenient ways for you to submit your undergraduate enrollment decision and make your $300 non-refundable deposit to secure your spot: Submit The Online Form (Day Undergraduate Only) Loading... Alvernia Enrollment Portal Complete your Confirmation of Enrollment Form online by logging into your Alvernia portal along with your $300 non-refundable enrollment deposit By completing this task, you are officially a Golden Wolf! Mail Check or Money Order Mail your check or money order (payable to Alvernia University) to: Office of Admissions Alvernia University 400 Saint Bernardine St. Reading, PA, 19607 Not Sure If This Page Is For You? If you are an adult, graduate or international student, this deposit page isn't for you. Please see the link below to secure your spot with the Pack: Graduate or Adult Education Student - Contact us at gradandadult@alvernia.edu or (610) 796-5187 to be connected to an Admissions Advisor. International Student What To Do After Submitting Your Deposit Visit the Admitted Students Guide Learn More Apply for Financial Aid Learn More Register for an Admissions Event Learn More Lead the Pack +1.888.258.3764 400 St. Bernardine Street, Reading, Pa. 19607 admissions@alvernia.edu Main Menu Directory Employment Privacy Policy Accessibility Site Map Alvernia's AI Recruiter Chat with Ashlee © 2026 Alvernia University"
