unity and Partners Find Us Contact Us Faculty/Staff Directory Maps & Directions Image Logins Image Academic Calendar Image Locations FIND IT Visit Apply Now Request Information Virtual Tour Logins Results See All About Directory Student Experience Athletics Maps Jobs at AU Programs Book Store Financial Aid & Tuition Make a Gift Recent News Sep 1, 2026 Alvernia University forms alliance with Independence Blue Cross to Expand Educational Opportunities The new relationship creates flexible, affordable pathways for Independence Blue Cross associates to earn undergraduate and graduate degrees while advancing their careers Alvernia University has joined … Aug 26, 2026 Alvernia’s Electrical and Mechanical Engineering Programs Receive ABET Accreditation Accreditation affirms that the university’s programs meet the quality standards established by the engineering professionAlvernia University’s Bachelor of Science programs in electrical engineering and mechanical… Aug 24, 2026 Alvernia President Fitzgerald featured in article about workplace adaptability Alvernia President Glynis A. Fitzgerald, Ph.D., was featured in \"Adaptability in the Workplace,\" an article written by Adam Mendler, a nationally recognized authority on leadership.\"Adaptability in the workplace is becoming… See All News Upcoming Events Data Analytics Virtual Information Session Achieve More With A Data Analytics… Thursday, Sep 10, 6:00 pm - 7:00 pm DPT Virtual Information Session Thursday, Sep 17, 6:00 pm - 7:00 pm Latinos Unidos: A Hispanic Heritage Month Celebration Register Here Theme: ¡Unidos, Somos Más! (Together, We Are One!)Location: Alvernia University, Francis Hall Atrium and Theatre, 400 Saint Bernardine Street, Reading, PA… Friday, Sep 25, 5:00 pm - 8:30 pm FAQs What type of financial aid is available? At Alvernia, applying for financial aid is easy. We encourage all prospective Alvernia students to apply, even if you feel you may not be eligible for assistance. The Office of Student Financial Services is available to answer questions and guide you through any financial aid situation, email us, call us at 610-796-8201 or stop by the office in Room 114 of Bernardine Hall. Read more financial aid, fees, FAFSA, and billing FAQs How do I Create My Comeback? At Alvernia, we’re in the business of supporting and affirming people in the pursuit of changing their lives for good. If the vision you have of your life includes making an impact on the world, up-leveling your career growth, building a better life for your family, serving your community, or becoming the leader you’ve always known yourself to be - join us to kick-start your next steps. You’re here to get ahead, we're here to help. Contact our knowledgeable admissions coordinators for more information at gradandadult@alvernia.edu , 610-796-5187 When will I receive housing information if I am an incoming first-year or transfer student? The Office of Residence Life will begin to communicate with incoming first-year and transfer students with complete detailed instructions by the end of February.  Our goal is to open the incoming student housing application no later than mid-March. When should I apply? The path to college is a process that typically starts in high school. Our Undergraduate Admissions Office is devoted to helping students and their families through this important and exciting time by arranging visits, hosting events, and answering questions to help you meet future goals and craft a fulfilling life. And, we want you to experience the many ways that Alvernia can help you do this! INQUIRE GIVE VISIT APPLY Breadcrumb Home Faculty & Staff Faculty & Staff Directory Faculty & Staff Directory Search Faculty & Staff Directory Search Department - Any - Academic Compliance Department Academic Success Center Addictions & Mental Health Treatment Aramark Collegiate Hospitality Athletic Training Athletics Bookstore Business Affairs Campus Operations Chemistry Clinical Counseling College of Health Sciences C