r of Physical Therapy program. ✔️ Explore the program and curriculum ✔️ Meet our expert faculty ✔️ Get your questions answered about requirements & the application process Whether you’re advancing your education after earning a bachelor’s degree or seeking an accelerated path, Alvernia University’s DPT program offers a comprehensive and compassionate learning experience tailored to your goals. Grad & Adult Admissions Learn more Rhapsody & Song Sep 18, 2026 7:30 PM - 9:30 PM Alvernia University, Francis Hall Theatre An evening of classical, jazz and Broadway music benefiting Alvernia's Hope Fund, which benefits students facing unexpected financial hardships. With special guest vocalist Glynis Fitzgerald, Ph.D., Alvernia University president. Arts & Culture Learn more Latinos Unidos: A Hispanic Heritage Month Celebration Sep 25, 2026 5:00 PM - 8:30 PM Alvernia University, Francis Hall Theatre Alvernia University’s O’Pake Institute for Economic Development and Entrepreneurship, through its Cultural Coalition, is proud to present Latinos Unidos: A Hispanic Heritage Month Celebration, an inspiring event that honors the rich cultures, traditions, achievements and enduring contributions of Hispanic and Latino communities. Multicultural Engagement Learn more Fall Open House I Sep 26, 2026 10:00 AM - 2:00 PM Whether you're just beginning your college search or getting ready to submit your application, our first Fall Open House is the perfect opportunity to experience the Alvernia community. During this open house, you'll learn more about our academic programs, the application process, connect with faculty and staff, hear firsthand from current students, and explore the many resources available to support your success. Our campus resource fair will showcase academic programs, student services, campus involvement opportunities, and more! The day will conclude with a major-specific campus tour, giving you a closer look at the spaces where you'll learn and grow, followed by lunch in the Student Center Dining Hall. No matter where you are in your college search journey, we invite you to take your first step into the Pack and discover what it means to be part of the Alvernia community! Admissions Learn more Fall 2026 Career Fair Sep 29, 2026 12:00 PM - 3:00 PM Alvernia University, The Plex Calling all employers, organizations and industry partners. The Office of Career Development at Alvernia invites you to network with university students to discuss full-time, part-time and internship opportunities. For more information, contact Director of Career Development Marc Goldman at marc.goldman@alvernia.edu or career.development@alvernia.edu. Career Development Learn more Physician Associate Virtual Information Session Oct 09, 2026 12:00 PM - 1:00 PM Zoom Virtual Event Join us for a virtual information session on October 9, where you’ll learn more about our Master of Medical Science in Physician Associate Studies program. ✔️ Explore the program and curriculum ✔️ Meet our expert faculty ✔️ Get your questions answered about requirements & the application process Grad & Adult Admissions Learn more Pagination Page 1 Next page ›› Hallmark Events Every year is filled with happenings across Alvernia's locations, but these annual traditions are extra special. Commencement Along with the annual celebration of Alvernia graduates, the university also stages an honors convocation, Baccalaureate mass, pinning ceremonies and a recognition event for senior athletes. Learn More Homecoming & Family Weekend Every fall, the Alvernia family reunites to mingle, cheer on the football team and participate in family-friendly events. Learn More Annual Happenings Alvernia has developed a number of traditions and yearly events since it opened in 1958 as a college for the Bernardine Franciscan Sisters. Learn More Venues Alvernia hosts athletic competitions, artistic events, conferences and much more at its locations. Francis Hall The oldest building on campus, Francis Hall serves as a hub of academic and social activity. Learn More The PLEX The Tom and Helen Flynn Complex for Recreation, Wellness and Health Sciences (PLEX) is a 100,000-square-foot academic and recreation hybrid facility. Learn More Physical Education Center The Physical Education Center hosts numerous athletic contests along with annual events such as Maroon and Gold Night. Learn More Find a New Experience Discover a new organization on PAX - Promoting Alvernia eXperiences. Visit the Site Lead the Pack +1.888.258.3764 400 St. Bernardine Street, Reading, Pa. 19607 admissions@alvernia.edu Main Menu Directory Employment Privacy Policy Accessibility Site Map Alvernia's AI Recruiter Chat with Ashlee © 2026 Alvernia University"
