nd Partners Find Us Contact Us Faculty/Staff Directory Maps & Directions Image Logins Image Academic Calendar Image Locations FIND IT Visit Apply Now Request Information Virtual Tour Logins Results See All About Directory Student Experience Athletics Maps Jobs at AU Programs Book Store Financial Aid & Tuition Make a Gift Recent News Sep 11, 2026 Alvernia Marks 25th Anniversary of Sept. 11 Through Service and Interfaith Remembrance University launches new Franciscan Fridays service series and gathers faith and community leaders to honor the lives lost and legacy of service  Alvernia University commemorated the 25th anniversary of… Sep 14, 2026 2026 Hispanic Heritage Month at Alvernia Celebrating Hispanic Heritage Month: September 15 to October 15Hispanic Heritage Month is celebrated every September to October. The month allows for individuals to celebrate the histories, cultures, and contributions of… Sep 1, 2026 Alvernia University forms alliance with Independence Blue Cross to Expand Educational Opportunities The new relationship creates flexible, affordable pathways for Independence Blue Cross associates to earn undergraduate and graduate degrees while advancing their careers Alvernia University has joined … See All News Upcoming Events DPT Virtual Information Session Sep 17 Thursday 2026 6:00 PM - 7:00 PM Rhapsody & Song Tickets are $25 and can be purchased online through Eventbrite or at the door.Meet the ArtistsDeanna Reuben, VocalsDeanna Reuben '79 has had an extensive vocal performance… Sep 18 Friday 2026 7:30 PM - 9:30 PM Latinos Unidos: A Hispanic Heritage Month Celebration Register Here Theme: ¡Unidos, Somos Más! (Together, We Are One!)Location: Alvernia University, Francis Hall Atrium and Theatre, 400 Saint Bernardine Street, Reading, PA…, Sep 25 Friday 2026 5:00 PM - 8:30 PM FAQs What type of financial aid is available? At Alvernia, applying for financial aid is easy. We encourage all prospective Alvernia students to apply, even if you feel you may not be eligible for assistance. The Office of Student Financial Services is available to answer questions and guide you through any financial aid situation, email us, call us at 610-796-8201 or stop by the office in Room 114 of Bernardine Hall. Read more financial aid, fees, FAFSA, and billing FAQs How do I Create My Comeback? At Alvernia, we’re in the business of supporting and affirming people in the pursuit of changing their lives for good. If the vision you have of your life includes making an impact on the world, up-leveling your career growth, building a better life for your family, serving your community, or becoming the leader you’ve always known yourself to be - join us to kick-start your next steps. You’re here to get ahead, we're here to help. Contact our knowledgeable admissions coordinators for more information at gradandadult@alvernia.edu , 610-796-5187 When will I receive housing information if I am an incoming first-year or transfer student? The Office of Residence Life will begin to communicate with incoming first-year and transfer students with complete detailed instructions by the end of February.  Our goal is to open the incoming student housing application no later than mid-March. When should I apply? The path to college is a process that typically starts in high school. Our Undergraduate Admissions Office is devoted to helping students and their families through this important and exciting time by arranging visits, hosting events, and answering questions to help you meet future goals and craft a fulfilling life. And, we want you to experience the many ways that Alvernia can help you do this! INQUIRE GIVE VISIT APPLY Breadcrumb Home The Franco Library The Franco Library The Franco Library Discover the wealth of resources and services at the Franco Library of Alvernia University, supporting students, faculty, and staff in their academic research and intellectual pursuits. Librarians instruct users in the access, evaluation and ethical use of information sources. They also work closely with faculty to plan the development of resources, information literacy instruction and research assistance that support self-initiation of lifelong-learning and fulfillment. The Franco Library Access Your Library Account Interlibrary Loan Library Forms Library Hours Library Policies Meet the Staff The Library Collection Databases Research Guides Library Catalog Reference Services How We Can Help The Dr. Frank A. Franco Library Learning Center librarians and staff work with faculty and students in a variety of ways to find and evaluate the information needed for research and coursework. The librarians welcome the opportunity to cooperate with faculty in integrating information literacy skills into the curriculum. Interested faculty members can contact the Information Literacy Librarian at 610-796-5019 to explore the content to be addressed by a librarian, and the most appropriate time to schedule one or more sessions with one of the librarians. The Library personnel are available to assist students and faculty on an individual basis with all aspects of searching and evaluating information. Students and faculty can contact us in a number of ways – whichever method is most convenient. Ask for assistance in the Library: Ask one of the librarians for assistance or ask for assistance at the Circulation Desk. Set up an appointment to meet with one of the Reference Librarians: Librarians are available to meet with students and faculty on an individual basis to discuss your information research needs and appropriate strategies for accessing the information. Please call 610 796-8223 to schedule an in-person or virtual appointment with one of the librarians. Ask your question by email: Reach a librarian at Alvernia.library@alvernia.edu Key Research Guides Citation Guide Research Quick Guide Copyright & Fair Use Avoiding Plagiarism Grammar & Writing YouTube Tutorial Videos Open Educational Resources Chat With A Librarian 24/7 Live chat with a librarian: Contact a librarian with questions instantly using our chat service. During Library Service hours, you’ll connect with an Alvernia librarian. Outside of business hours, you’ll be connected with librarians from our partner libraries in PA. Chat Contact Us Phone : 610-796-8223 Research : 610-796-5019 Email : Alvernia.library@alvernia.edu Lead the Pack +1.888.258.3764 400 St. Bernardine Street, Reading, Pa. 19607 admissions@alvernia.edu Main Menu Directory Employment Privacy Policy Accessibility Site Map Alvernia's AI Recruiter Chat with Ashlee © 2026 Alvernia University"
    },
