munity and Partners Find Us Contact Us Faculty/Staff Directory Maps & Directions Image Logins Image Academic Calendar Image Locations FIND IT Visit Apply Now Request Information Virtual Tour Logins Results See All About Directory Student Experience Athletics Maps Jobs at AU Programs Book Store Financial Aid & Tuition Make a Gift Recent News Sep 11, 2026 Alvernia Marks 25th Anniversary of Sept. 11 Through Service and Interfaith Remembrance University launches new Franciscan Fridays service series and gathers faith and community leaders to honor the lives lost and legacy of service  Alvernia University commemorated the 25th anniversary of… Sep 14, 2026 2026 Hispanic Heritage Month at Alvernia Celebrating Hispanic Heritage Month: September 15 to October 15Hispanic Heritage Month is celebrated every September to October. The month allows for individuals to celebrate the histories, cultures, and contributions of… Sep 1, 2026 Alvernia University forms alliance with Independence Blue Cross to Expand Educational Opportunities The new relationship creates flexible, affordable pathways for Independence Blue Cross associates to earn undergraduate and graduate degrees while advancing their careers Alvernia University has joined … See All News Upcoming Events DPT Virtual Information Session Sep 17 Thursday 2026 6:00 PM - 7:00 PM Rhapsody & Song Tickets are $25 and can be purchased online through Eventbrite or at the door.Meet the ArtistsDeanna Reuben, VocalsDeanna Reuben '79 has had an extensive vocal performance… Sep 18 Friday 2026 7:30 PM - 9:30 PM Latinos Unidos: A Hispanic Heritage Month Celebration Register Here Theme: ¡Unidos, Somos Más! (Together, We Are One!)Location: Alvernia University, Francis Hall Atrium and Theatre, 400 Saint Bernardine Street, Reading, PA…, Sep 25 Friday 2026 5:00 PM - 8:30 PM FAQs What type of financial aid is available? At Alvernia, applying for financial aid is easy. We encourage all prospective Alvernia students to apply, even if you feel you may not be eligible for assistance. The Office of Student Financial Services is available to answer questions and guide you through any financial aid situation, email us, call us at 610-796-8201 or stop by the office in Room 114 of Bernardine Hall. Read more financial aid, fees, FAFSA, and billing FAQs How do I Create My Comeback? At Alvernia, we’re in the business of supporting and affirming people in the pursuit of changing their lives for good. If the vision you have of your life includes making an impact on the world, up-leveling your career growth, building a better life for your family, serving your community, or becoming the leader you’ve always known yourself to be - join us to kick-start your next steps. You’re here to get ahead, we're here to help. Contact our knowledgeable admissions coordinators for more information at gradandadult@alvernia.edu , 610-796-5187 When will I receive housing information if I am an incoming first-year or transfer student? The Office of Residence Life will begin to communicate with incoming first-year and transfer students with complete detailed instructions by the end of February.  Our goal is to open the incoming student housing application no later than mid-March. When should I apply? The path to college is a process that typically starts in high school. Our Undergraduate Admissions Office is devoted to helping students and their families through this important and exciting time by arranging visits, hosting events, and answering questions to help you meet future goals and craft a fulfilling life. And, we want you to experience the many ways that Alvernia can help you do this! INQUIRE GIVE VISIT APPLY Breadcrumb Home Sustainability at Alvernia Sustainability at Alvernia Sustainability at Alvernia Alvernia University has always demonstrated a respect and appreciation for the environment and their community, and humbly continues to do so. With dedicated faculty, staff, students and community members, who share adoration and respect for nature, Alvernia is committed to its role in environmental protection, appreciation and solutions. The university creates interdisciplinary projects and solutions to cater to all aspects of sustainability: social, cultural, economic or environmental. Sustainability at Alvernia About the Office of Institutional Sustainability Bog Turtle Creek Farm Community Sustainability EcoHouse Faculty and Staff Sustainability Student Sustainability Alvernia's Sustainability Plan Alvernia supports all 17 United Nations Sustainable Development Goals. Five goals in particular align well with the University’s mission and endeavors. Good Health and Wellbeing – Student, staff, and faculty wellbeing is a top priority for the university. Physical and mental health is an important factor to consider to create an inclusive environment within the university and city as a whole. Alvernia has an incoming regional bike share program and an extensive trail system that support both physical and mental wellbeing. Freshens at the PLEX is a popular healthy dining option that focus on local, healthy, intuitive eating. Quality Education – The University has several colleges and a number of majors to ensure a quality education in numerous fields. Faculty is thoroughly chosen and a hands-on experiential learning journey is provided to all students. Decent Work and Economic Growth – The University strives to provide all faculty and staff living wages and benefits. The student, faculty, and staff contributions to the University and greater Reading promotes job creation and economic stimulation. The University educates students and provides them with the tools to become leaders in the workforce and think creatively in different industries. Reduced Inequalities – Alvernia prioritizes environmental and community justice in all aspects of the University’s educational and leadership experience. The university has several long running initiatives like the Bog Turtle Creek Farm and Clare’s Cupboard that focus on affordable and accessible food and resources. More recent initiatives include the creation of the Office of Mission, Diversity, and Inclusion. Sustainable Cities and Communities –With new CollegeTowne endeavors, the University is more intertwined with the city than ever. With projects involving bike shares and accessible transportation, continuation of Bog Turtle Creek Farm and selling affordable produce to low-income families, and the Angelica Creek Park which provides a natural space for students and the community to enjoy, Alvernia is a part of Reading as much as the city is a part of Alvernia. Student Sustainability There are a variety of ways that students can get involved with sustainability at Alvernia, including employment, academic programs, sustainability trips and student organizations. Learn More Faculty and Staff Sustainability Faculty and staff actively participate in sustainability at Alvernia in many ways. Learn More Community Sustainability Alvernia is committed to engaging with the surrounding community on sustainability initiatives, aiming to create a more sustainable community for current and future members. Learn More EcoHouse The EcoHouse offers a variety of student experiential learning opportunities from which students can gain real-world experience to help equip them as emerging leaders with the mindset and skillset to tackle our communities' sustainability challenges successfully. Learn More Lead the Pack +1.888.258.3764 400 St. Bernardine Street, Reading, Pa. 19607 admissions@alvernia.edu Main Menu Directory Employment Privacy Policy Accessibility Site Map Alvernia's AI Recruiter Chat with Ashlee © 2026 Alvernia University"
    },
