      "description": "Discover Greater Reading | Alvernia University Skip to main content Main navigation Find it About About Who We Are A Franciscan Tradition Rankings & Facts History & Timeline Leadership Mission & Ministry University Information Work at Alvernia Community Engagement CollegeTowne Holleran Center for Community & Global Engagement O'Pake Institute Total Experience Learning Locations Points of Pride Sustainability Culture of Care Network Caring Faculty Ethical Leadership Service Minded Perfectly Located Image News Image Events Image Success Stories Academics Academics Find Your Program Undergraduate Majors Graduate Programs Accelerated Adult Bachelor Programs Online Programs Colleges and Schools Seniors College Experience Learning Apprenticeship to Degree Career Development Experiential Learning O’Pake Fellows SURF Program Holleran Service Opportunities Image Academic Calendar Image Catalog and Handbooks Image Franco Library Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Admission Pathways How to Apply Undergraduate Graduate Adult Education International Corporate Partnerships Military & Veterans Transfer Financial Aid Student Financial Services Tuition & Residential Costs FAFSA: What You Need to Know Scholarships & Awards Visit Campus Graduate, Adult & Continuing Studies Undergraduate Image Apply Now Image Check Application Status Image Request Info Student Experience Student Experience Our Campus Living on Campus Dining Options Our Community Things to Do in the Area Experiences Get Involved Athletics & Recreation Student Organizations and Activities Commuters International Experiences Support SOLAR (Support, Opportunity, Love, Access, Resources) Initiative Academic Support Medical & Counseling Center Community Resources Mission & Ministry Office of Career Development Image Bookstore Image Arts & Culture Image Athletics Resources Resources Information For... Future Students New and First-Year Students Graduate and Adult Students Alumni Parents and Families Community and Partners Find Us Contact Us Faculty/Staff Directory Maps & Directions Image Logins Image Academic Calendar Image Locations FIND IT Visit Apply Now Request Information Virtual Tour Logins Results See All About Directory Student Experience Athletics Maps Jobs at AU Programs Book Store Financial Aid & Tuition Make a Gift Recent News Sep 11, 2026 Alvernia Marks 25th Anniversary of Sept. 11 Through Service and Interfaith Remembrance University launches new Franciscan Fridays service series and gathers faith and community leaders to honor the lives lost and legacy of service  Alvernia University commemorated the 25th anniversary of… Sep 14, 2026 2026 Hispanic Heritage Month at Alvernia Celebrating Hispanic Heritage Month: September 15 to October 15Hispanic Heritage Month is celebrated every September to October. The month allows for individuals to celebrate the histories, cultures, and contributions of… Sep 1, 2026 Alvernia University forms alliance with Independence Blue Cross to Expand Educational Opportunities The new relationship creates flexible, affordable pathways for Independence Blue Cross associates to earn undergraduate and graduate degrees while advancing their careers Alvernia University has joined … See All News Upcoming Events DPT Virtual Information Session Sep 17 Thursday 2026 6:00 PM - 7:00 PM Rhapsody & Song Tickets are $25 and can be purchased online through Eventbrite or at the door.Meet the ArtistsDeanna Reuben, VocalsDeanna Reuben '79 has had an extensive vocal performance… Sep 18 Friday 2026 7:30 PM - 9:30 PM Latinos Unidos: A Hispanic Heritage Month Celebration Register Here Theme: ¡Unidos, Somos Más! (Together, We Are One!)Location: Alvernia University, Francis Hall Atrium and Theatre, 400 Saint Bernardine Street, Reading, PA…, Sep 25 Friday 2026 5:00 PM - 8:30 PM FAQs What type of financial aid is available? At Alvernia, applying for financial aid is easy. We encourage all prospective Alvernia students to apply, even if you feel you may not be eligible for assistance. The Office of Student Financial Services is available to answer questions and guide you through any financial aid situation, email us, call us at 610-796-8201 or stop by the office in Room 114 of Bernardine Hall. Read more financial aid, fees, FAFSA, and billing FAQs How do I Create My Comeback? At Alvernia, we’re in the business of supporting and affirming people in the pursuit of changing their lives for good. If the vision you have of your life includes making an impact on the world, up-leveling your career growth, building a better life for your family, serving your community, or becoming the leader you’ve always known yourself to be - join us to kick-start your next steps. You’re here to get ahead, we're here to help. Contact our knowledgeable admissions coordinators for more information at gradandadult@alvernia.edu , 610-796-5187 When will I receive housing information if I am an incoming first-year or transfer student? The Office of Residence Life will begin to communicate with incoming first-year and transfer students with complete detailed instructions by the end of February.  Our goal is to open the incoming student housing application no later than mid-March. When should I apply? The path to college is a process that typically starts in high school. Our Undergraduate Admissions Office is devoted to helping students and their families through this important and exciting time by arranging visits, hosting events, and answering questions to help you meet future goals and craft a fulfilling life. And, we want you to experience the many ways that Alvernia can help you do this! INQUIRE GIVE VISIT APPLY Breadcrumb Home Discover Greater Reading Discover Greater Reading Discover Greater Reading Greater Reading has a rich cultural heritage made famous by early Amish and German settlers. Today, Reading is a culturally diverse city surrounded by quaint neighborhoods and scenic outdoor destinations. There is an abundance of things to see and do in the region. Greater Reading is home to multiple venues offering concerts, shows and sporting events; a thriving food and beverage scene; seasonal festivals; a sprawling community arts center and much more. Learn More Request More Info Apply Visit Us Things To Do Explore Events Sights to See Attractions in Reading Where to Eat Area Restaurants Where To Stay Lodging in Berks County Lead the Pack +1.888.258.3764 400 St. Bernardine Street, Reading, Pa. 19607 admissions@alvernia.edu Main Menu Directory Employment Privacy Policy Accessibility Site Map Alvernia's AI Recruiter Chat with Ashlee © 2026 Alvernia University"
    },
