are additional resources available in the surrounding community. CLICK TO JUMP TO A RESOURCE • 211/Find Help • Advocacy and Referral • Child Care Assistance/WIC • Clothing • Community Action Programs • Crisis Support • Domestic Violence • Drop-In Centers • Emergency Resources • Employment Assistance • Food Assistance • Government Assistance • Health and Wellness • Hotlines and Emergency Contacts • Housing/Utility Assistance • Identification • Immigration and Legal Aid • Legal • LGBTQ Resources • Libraries • Mental Health Services • Resource Guides • Self-Help and Support Groups • Temporary Employment Agencies • Transportation • Utilities • Veterans Resources 211/Find Help Get Help - PA 211 • Description: Find emergency shelters, housing/utility assistance, healthcare, food assistance, mental health services, community resources and more closest to your ZIP code. • Web: pa211.org/get-help Findhelp.org • Description: Search and connect to social care. Find resources for food, housing and more. • Web: findhelp.org Advocacy and Referral The Arc Alliance Advocacy Services • Address: 3075 Ridge Pike, Eaglesville, PA • Phone: 610-265-4700 • Web: thearcalliance.org Area Agency on Aging • Address: 633 Court St., Eighth Floor, Reading, PA • Phone: 610-478-6500 • Web: berkspa.gov/departments/aging Berks Aid Network • Address: 429 Walnut St., Reading, PA • Phone: 610-375-6523 • Web: cocounty.org/services/ Berks Children and Youth Services • Address: 633 Court St., 11th Floor, Reading, PA • Phone: 610-478-6700 • Web: berkspa.gov/departments/children-and-youth Centro Hispano Hispanic Center • Address: 501 Washington St., Reading, PA • Phone: 610-685-1265 • Web: centrohispano.org Council on Chemical Abuse • Address: 50 N. Fifth St., Reading, PA • Phone: 610-376-8669 • Web: cocaberks.org Disability Rights Network of PA • Address: 301 Chestnut St., Suite 300, Harrisburg, PA • Phone: 717-236-8110 • Web: disabilityrightspa.org Greater Reading Mental Health Alliance • Address: 1234 Pen