ng, PA • Phone: 610-685-4523 • Web: lifelineofberks.org Mary's Shelter • Description: Maternity home, support, diaper bank • Address: 615 Kenhorst Blvd., Reading, PA • Phone: 610-376-1973 • Website: marysshelter.org Pennsylvania WIC • Description: The Pennsylvania Special Supplemental Nutrition Program for Women, Infants and Children (WIC) provides nutrition services, breastfeeding support, health care and social service referrals, and healthy foods. • Website: wic.health.pa.gov/pawic Service Access & Management Inc. Description: Early Intervention Address: 19 N. Sixth St., Reading, PA Phone: 610-236-0530 Website: sam-inc.org Chester County/Coatesville Resources The Wardrobe Description: Free career closet • Appointments in Kennett Square and Exton (Chester County) as well as Norristown, Upper Darby, and Philadelphia • 1 on 1 Coaching appointments Website: careerwardrobe.org Chester County Food Bank Website: chestercountyfoodbank.org • Location in Exton, Pa., about 20 minutes from Coatesville. CYWA (Community Youth & Women’s Alliance) Description: Food distribution program, shelter and housing programs. Website: cywa.org Adult Tutoring - Chester County Library System & Chester County OIC Description: Adult tutoring program: reading, writing, spelling, ESL Website: chescolibraries.org/using-the-library/adult-tutoring-program-oic/ Chester County Library System Description: Mobile Hotspots $2/day for 3 or 7 days - available at the Exton branch. Website: ccls.org Clothing Catholic Charities • Address: 400 Washington St., Reading, PA • Phone: 610-376-7144 • Web: catholiccharitiesad.org Clothing Programs in Philadelphia • Web: Learn more . Clothing Programs in Pottsville • Web: findhelp.org/goods/clothing--pottsville-pa CommunityAid Thrift Store and Donation Center • Address: 5370 Allentown Pike, Temple, PA • Phone: 717-412-7706 Goodwill • Address: 602 E. Lancaster Ave., Reading, PA • Phone: 610-777-5250 • Web: yourgoodwill.org Hope Rescue Mission Thrift Store • Address: 745 N. Sixth St., Reading, PA • Phone: 610-375-4224 • Web: hopeforreading.org/donateitems New Journey Community Outreach Inc. • Address: 138 S Sixth St., Reading, PA • Phone: 610-375-2662 • Web: njcoinc.org Our Closet in Your Neighborhood - Jewish Family and Children's Service of Greater Philadelphia • Phone: 866-532-7669 • Web: jfcsphilly.org/our-closet-in-your-neighborhood Plato's Closet • Description: Buys and sells gently used clothes, shoes and accessories. • Address: 1183 Berkshire Blvd, Wyomissing, PA • Phone: 484-709-2812 Spring Valley Church of God • Address: 2727 Old Pricetown Road, Temple, PA • Phone: 610-929-7969 • Web: springvalley.church Community Action Programs Berks Community Action Program • Web: bcapberks.org Office of Community Empowerment and Opportunity - Philadelphia • Web: phila.gov/departments/office-of-community-empowerment-and-opportunity Schuylkill Community Action • Web: schuylkillcommunityaction.com Crisis Support 988 Lifeline • Description: 988 is a national suicide and crisis lifeline. • Phone : 988 • Web: 988lifeline.org American Foundation For Suicide Prevention Support Groups • Description: AFSP lists U.S. and international suicide bereavement support groups as a public service to loss survivors. • Web: afsp.org/find-a-support-group Crisis Text Line • Description: Free confidential 24/7 support at your fingertips. • Phone: Text HOME to 741741 to connect with a volunteer crisis counselor • Web: crisistextline.org Department of Behavioral Health & Intellectual disability services • Description: DBHIDS operates a 24-hour call center to assist people and their families with behavioral health crises. • Phone: 215-686-4420 • Web: dbhids.org Holcomb Behavioral Health Systems • Description: Holcomb Behavioral Health Systems provides a comprehensive range of services and supports for people with mental health, substance abuse, intellectual and developmental disabilities, and co-occurring disorders. • Web: chimes.org/about/chimes-family/holcomb-behavioral-health-systems Mental Health America Warmline • Description: A warmline is a phone number you call to have a conversation with someone who can provide support during hard times. Warmlines are staffed by trained peers who have been through their own mental health struggles and know what it’s like to need help. • Web: warmline.org/#directory Penn Medicine - Alvernia Medical and Counseling Center • Address : 421 Adams St., Reading, PA • Phone: 610-568-1467 • Web: alvernia.edu/current-students/medical-and-counseling-center Schuylkill County Crisis Intervention • Description: Crisis Intervention provides mental health intervention, assessment, support, screening, and referral services 24 hours a day, 7 days a week. • Phone: 877-993-4357 • Text: 63288 • Web: ccrinfo.org/schuylkill-county The Trevor Project • Description: The Trevor Project is the leading suicide prevention and crisis intervention nonprofit organization for LGBTQ+ young people. We provide information & support to LGBTQ+ young people 24/7, all year round. • Text: 678-678 • Phone: 1-866-488-7386 • Web: thetrevorproject.org Domestic Violence National Domestic Violence Hotline • Phone: 1-800-799-7233 • Web: thehotline.org Pennsylvania Coalition Against Domestic Violence • Web: pcadv.org Philadelphia Domestic Violence Hotline • Web: womenagainstabuse.org/get-help/pdvh-2-2 Safe Berks • Address: 255 Chestnut St., Reading, PA • Phone: 610-373-1206 • Web: safeberks.org Schuylkill Hope Center for Victims of Domestic Violence in Pottsville • Phone: 570-622-6220 • Web: domesticshelters.org/help/pa/pottsville Drop-In Centers Dimplez4days Programs - Philadelphia Nonprofit • Description: This safe haven after-school environment aims to provide a haven for Philadelphia children and youth, providing a nurturing environment, building positive relations between residents and decreasing violence in the community between 3 and 8 p.m. • Phone: 267-325-5138 • Web: dimplez4dayz.org U-Turn (Family Promise of Berks County) • Description: This program offers case management and drop-in center facilities on Tuesdays and Thursdays from 2 to 5 p.m. to unaccompanied/homeless youth in Berks County. It is designed to help individuals achieve educational, employment and housing stabilization goals. • Address: 325 N. Fifth St., Reading, PA • Phone: 610-373-3323 • Web: familypromiseofberks.org/u-turn Mary’s Shelter Drop-In Center Residential Program • Description: Available after school for youth from ages 14-21 from 3:30 to 6:30 p.m. Mondays through Fridays. Features a laundry room, gym equipment, recreational activities, a full kitchen and a computer lab for school/job/recreational activities. • Address: 615 Kenhorst Blvd., Reading, PA • Phone: 610-376-1973 • Web: marysshelter.org/residential Emergency Resources Emergency Resources Guide This guide can help you find and access resources for a variety of basic needs , including food, housing, healthcare, legal assistance, and more, particularly in case of emergencies or situations that necessitate off-campus support. Employment Assistance Berks Community Action Program • Address: 645 Penn St., Reading, PA • Phone: 610-376-6571 • Web: bcapberks.org Berkshire Personnel Network • Address: 1015 Rockland St., Reading, PA • Phone: 610-288-1448 • Web: trsinc.org/services/business-and-industry-berks-county/berks-personnel-network Community Skills Program Counseling and Rehabilitation • Address: 1150 Berkshire Blvd # 210, Wyomissing, PA • Phone: 610-276-3380 Office of Vocational Rehabilitation • Address: 3602 Kutztown Road, Reading, PA • Phone: 610-621-5800 PA Careerlink of Berks County • Address: 1920 Kutztown Road, Reading, PA • Phone: 610-988-1300 • Web: careerlinkberks.com PeopleShare Pottsville • Description: Temporary, temp-to-hire, and direct hire staffing • Web: peopleshareworks.com/pottsville Philly Temps & Perm • Description: Administrative and event staffing agency serving Philadelphia and the surrounding suburbs. • Web: phillytemps.com Food Assistance Find Food Assistance in Berks County • Description: A comprehensive directory of food pantries. • Web: foodpantries.org/co/pa-berks Food Map - Helping Harvest • Address: 117 Morgan Drive, Reading, PA • Phone: 610-926-5802 • Web: helpingharvest.org/food-map Food Resources for Philadelphians • Web: phila.gov/2024-07-23-food-housing-resources-for-philadelphians Food Resources for Schuylkill County • Web: schuylkillcommunityaction.com/services/pantry Berks County WIC • Address: 1110C Rockland Road, Reading, PA • Phone: 610-373-5545 • Web: mfhs.org Berks Encore • Address: 40 N. Ninth St., Reading, PA • Phone: 610-374-3195 • Web: berksencore.org Birdsboro Nazarene Church • Address: 715 E. Third St., Reading, PA • Phone: 610-582-4700 • Web: birdsboronaz.org City Reach Church's Faith • Address: 1011A Cotton St., Reading, PA • Phone: 610-621-5227 Conrad Weiser Food Pantry • Address: 108 S. Robeson St., Robesonia, PA • Phone: 610-393-8313 • Web: trinityrobesonia.org Exeter Bible Fellowship Church • Address: 926 Philadelphia Terrace, Birdsboro, PA • Phone: 610-582-4191 • Web: exeterbfc.org Faith United Evangelical Lutheran Church • Address: 357 Walnut St., Denver, PA • Phone: 717-336-2141 • Web: faithunited-elca.org/give-2 Friend, Inc. • Address: 658D Noble St., Kutztown, PA • Phone: 610-683-7790 • Web: www.friendinc.org Hope Rescue Mission • Address: 645 North Sixth St., Reading, PA • Phone: 610-375-4224 • Web: hopeforreading.org Kennedy House • Address: 532 Spruce St., Reading, PA • Phone: 610-378-1947 New Journey Community Outreach • Address: 138 S. Sixth St., Reading, PA • Phone: 610-375-2662 • Web: www.njcoinc.org Salvation Army Of Reading • Address: 301 S. Fifth St., Reading, PA • Phone: 610-373-5208 • Web: salvationarmyreading.org Spring Valley Church of God • Address: 2727 Old Pricetown Road, Temple, PA • Phone: 610-929-7969 • Web: springvalley.church Trinity U.C.C. In His Name • Address: 2449 Cumberland Ave., Mount Penn, PA • Phone: 484-509-0706 • W