 and Partners Find Us Contact Us Faculty/Staff Directory Maps & Directions Image Logins Image Academic Calendar Image Locations FIND IT Visit Apply Now Request Information Virtual Tour Logins Results See All About Directory Student Experience Athletics Maps Jobs at AU Programs Book Store Financial Aid & Tuition Make a Gift Recent News Sep 11, 2026 Alvernia Marks 25th Anniversary of Sept. 11 Through Service and Interfaith Remembrance University launches new Franciscan Fridays service series and gathers faith and community leaders to honor the lives lost and legacy of service  Alvernia University commemorated the 25th anniversary of… Sep 14, 2026 2026 Hispanic Heritage Month at Alvernia Celebrating Hispanic Heritage Month: September 15 to October 15Hispanic Heritage Month is celebrated every September to October. The month allows for individuals to celebrate the histories, cultures, and contributions of… Sep 1, 2026 Alvernia University forms alliance with Independence Blue Cross to Expand Educational Opportunities The new relationship creates flexible, affordable pathways for Independence Blue Cross associates to earn undergraduate and graduate degrees while advancing their careers Alvernia University has joined … See All News Upcoming Events DPT Virtual Information Session Sep 17 Thursday 2026 6:00 PM - 7:00 PM Rhapsody & Song Tickets are $25 and can be purchased online through Eventbrite or at the door.Meet the ArtistsDeanna Reuben, VocalsDeanna Reuben '79 has had an extensive vocal performance… Sep 18 Friday 2026 7:30 PM - 9:30 PM Latinos Unidos: A Hispanic Heritage Month Celebration Register Here Theme: ¡Unidos, Somos Más! (Together, We Are One!)Location: Alvernia University, Francis Hall Atrium and Theatre, 400 Saint Bernardine Street, Reading, PA…, Sep 25 Friday 2026 5:00 PM - 8:30 PM FAQs What type of financial aid is available? At Alvernia, applying for financial aid is easy. We encourage all prospective Alvernia students to apply, even if you feel you may not be eligible for assistance. The Office of Student Financial Services is available to answer questions and guide you through any financial aid situation, email us, call us at 610-796-8201 or stop by the office in Room 114 of Bernardine Hall. Read more financial aid, fees, FAFSA, and billing FAQs How do I Create My Comeback? At Alvernia, we’re in the business of supporting and affirming people in the pursuit of changing their lives for good. If the vision you have of your life includes making an impact on the world, up-leveling your career growth, building a better life for your family, serving your community, or becoming the leader you’ve always known yourself to be - join us to kick-start your next steps. You’re here to get ahead, we're here to help. Contact our knowledgeable admissions coordinators for more information at gradandadult@alvernia.edu , 610-796-5187 When will I receive housing information if I am an incoming first-year or transfer student? The Office of Residence Life will begin to communicate with incoming first-year and transfer students with complete detailed instructions by the end of February.  Our goal is to open the incoming student housing application no later than mid-March. When should I apply? The path to college is a process that typically starts in high school. Our Undergraduate Admissions Office is devoted to helping students and their families through this important and exciting time by arranging visits, hosting events, and answering questions to help you meet future goals and craft a fulfilling life. And, we want you to experience the many ways that Alvernia can help you do this! INQUIRE GIVE VISIT APPLY Breadcrumb Home High School Students High School Students High School Students Get An Early Start on a Golden Opportunity At Alvernia University, the journey to graduating as a Golden Wolf begins well before Move-In Day. There are many opportunities for students to explore academic interests, interact with faculty and staff, and earn college credits while in high school. Scholarships and Awards Learn about the merit-based scholarships and awards Alvernia offers to qualified first-year applicants. FAFSA: What You Need To Know Stay up to date on the latest from federal student aid . Undergraduate Admissions Alvernia encourages you to schedule a visit to see Alvernia for yourself and meet the Admissions team . Dual Enrollment Program Alvernia's Dual Credit and Pre-College programs allow high school students to earn college credits. Upcoming Events Summer Open Houses The undergraduate admissions office invites you and your family to an open house which offers unique experiences depending on where you are in the college search process. Every open house is strategically different to offer more detailed information as the year progresses. • Learn More Individual Visits No matter where you are in the college search and enrollment process, visiting campus is the best way to see if Alvernia is the place you'd like to call home! • Learn More Majors and Minors Alvernia offers over 60 undergraduate programs of study . Experiential Learning Experiential learning ensures Alvernia students can step into their roles in a rapidly evolving job market on day one. SOLAR Alvernia's SOLAR (Support, Opportunity, Love, Access, and Resources) defines a campus culture of care. Organizations and Activities Through dozens of campus organizations and activities , Alvernia students hone lifetime skills essential for any industry or field of study. Merit Pages Alvernia uses Merit to create thousands of personalized stories to celebrate and publicize the great things done by our students. Get Inspired Undergraduate Admissions Alvernia encourages you to schedule a visit to see Alvernia for yourself and meet the Admissions team. Discover Alvernia Athletics Alvernia's Golden Wolves compete at the NCAA Division III level. Over 600 student-athletes competed in 29 team sports during the 2025-26 school year. Learn More Lead the Pack +1.888.258.3764 400 St. Bernardine Street, Reading, Pa. 19607 admissions@alvernia.edu Main Menu Directory Employment Privacy Policy Accessibility Site Map Alvernia's AI Recruiter Chat with Ashlee © 2026 Alvernia University"
    },
