nd Partners Find Us Contact Us Faculty/Staff Directory Maps & Directions Image Logins Image Academic Calendar Image Locations FIND IT Visit Apply Now Request Information Virtual Tour Logins Results See All About Directory Student Experience Athletics Maps Jobs at AU Programs Book Store Financial Aid & Tuition Make a Gift Recent News Sep 11, 2026 Alvernia Marks 25th Anniversary of Sept. 11 Through Service and Interfaith Remembrance University launches new Franciscan Fridays service series and gathers faith and community leaders to honor the lives lost and legacy of service  Alvernia University commemorated the 25th anniversary of… Sep 14, 2026 2026 Hispanic Heritage Month at Alvernia Celebrating Hispanic Heritage Month: September 15 to October 15Hispanic Heritage Month is celebrated every September to October. The month allows for individuals to celebrate the histories, cultures, and contributions of… Sep 1, 2026 Alvernia University forms alliance with Independence Blue Cross to Expand Educational Opportunities The new relationship creates flexible, affordable pathways for Independence Blue Cross associates to earn undergraduate and graduate degrees while advancing their careers Alvernia University has joined … See All News Upcoming Events DPT Virtual Information Session Sep 17 Thursday 2026 6:00 PM - 7:00 PM Rhapsody & Song Tickets are $25 and can be purchased online through Eventbrite or at the door.Meet the ArtistsDeanna Reuben, VocalsDeanna Reuben '79 has had an extensive vocal performance… Sep 18 Friday 2026 7:30 PM - 9:30 PM Latinos Unidos: A Hispanic Heritage Month Celebration Register Here Theme: ¡Unidos, Somos Más! (Together, We Are One!)Location: Alvernia University, Francis Hall Atrium and Theatre, 400 Saint Bernardine Street, Reading, PA…, Sep 25 Friday 2026 5:00 PM - 8:30 PM FAQs What type of financial aid is available? At Alvernia, applying for financial aid is easy. We encourage all prospective Alvernia students to apply, even if you feel you may not be eligible for assistance. The Office of Student Financial Services is available to answer questions and guide you through any financial aid situation, email us, call us at 610-796-8201 or stop by the office in Room 114 of Bernardine Hall. Read more financial aid, fees, FAFSA, and billing FAQs How do I Create My Comeback? At Alvernia, we’re in the business of supporting and affirming people in the pursuit of changing their lives for good. If the vision you have of your life includes making an impact on the world, up-leveling your career growth, building a better life for your family, serving your community, or becoming the leader you’ve always known yourself to be - join us to kick-start your next steps. You’re here to get ahead, we're here to help. Contact our knowledgeable admissions coordinators for more information at gradandadult@alvernia.edu , 610-796-5187 When will I receive housing information if I am an incoming first-year or transfer student? The Office of Residence Life will begin to communicate with incoming first-year and transfer students with complete detailed instructions by the end of February.  Our goal is to open the incoming student housing application no later than mid-March. When should I apply? The path to college is a process that typically starts in high school. Our Undergraduate Admissions Office is devoted to helping students and their families through this important and exciting time by arranging visits, hosting events, and answering questions to help you meet future goals and craft a fulfilling life. And, we want you to experience the many ways that Alvernia can help you do this! INQUIRE GIVE VISIT APPLY Breadcrumb Home Parents & Families Parents & Families Parents & Families Request More Info Apply Visit Us You have guided your child through many major life moments, and now is the time to help them navigate another major event — going to college. Whether this is your first time through the process or your 10th, you are bound to have questions. Please use us as a resource to help you along the way. Parents generally have questions about the following topics, so browse these areas of our site for information: Career Services Penn Medicine - Alvernia Medical and Counseling Center | Health Alerts Housing Options Contact Alvernia Parent Ambassadors Are you looking for ways to get involved at Alvernia? The university’s success is dependent on the people of our community and there are many meaningful opportunities for parent involvement. Consider becoming a Parent Ambassador and participate in one or more of the following ways: Accepted Students Day Welcome and talk with our prospective parents & students. Represent Alvernia at College Fair Lend a hand at a college fair in your neighborhood. Tag team with one of our Admissions’ Counselors or with another Alvernia volunteer. Volunteer at June Connection Days and/or August New Student Orientation (Move-In Day) Welcome and talk with our incoming parents & students. Help them get settled into their home away from home. Host A Welcome to Alvernia Reception in Your Region Partner with the Office of Alumni & Parent Engagement to plan an event to welcome and introduce our newest Golden Wolves and their families. (Summer Send-Offs) Homecoming & Family Weekend Offer your ideas and assistance in planning events/programs for parents. Letter-Writing Campaign Write a letter of reassurance to accepted students encouraging them to enroll at Alvernia or send welcome notes to first-year parents. Share Your Career Expertise Serve as an interviewer for Mock Interview Mania, Host a student(s) during Take A Golden Wolf to Work Week, or Provide internship, externship and job opportunities. Be A Recruiter Share your student’s and your Alvernia experience with friends, neighbors and acquaintances in your community, at work etc. Support Alvernia A gift will enhance your student’s education and future students. Recent News Alvernia Marks 25th Anniversary of Sept. 11 Through Service and Interfaith Remembrance University launches new Franciscan Fridays service series and gathers faith and community leaders to honor the lives lost and legacy of service Learn more 2026 Hispanic Heritage Month at Alvernia Learn more Alvernia University forms alliance with Independence Blue Cross to Expand Educational Opportunities The new relationship creates flexible, affordable pathways for IBX associates to earn undergraduate and graduate degrees while advancing their careers Read more See All News Upcoming Events DPT Virtual Information Session Sep 17, 2026 6:00 PM - 7:00 PM Zoom Virtual Event Join us for a virtual information session on September 17, where you’ll learn more about our Doctor of Physical Therapy program. ✔️ Explore the program and curriculum ✔️ Meet our expert faculty ✔️ Get your questions answered about requirements & the application process Whether you’re advancing your education after earning a bachelor’s degree or seeking an accelerated path, Alvernia University’s DPT program offers a comprehensive and compassionate learning experience tailored to your goals. Grad & Adult Admissions Learn more Rhapsody & Song Sep 18, 2026 7:30 PM - 9:30 PM Alvernia University, Francis Hall Theatre An evening of classical, jazz and Broadway music benefiting Alvernia's Hope Fund, which benefits students facing unexpected financial hardships. With special guest vocalist Glynis Fitzgerald, Ph.D., Alvernia University president. Arts & Culture Learn more Latinos Unidos: A Hispanic Heritage Month Celebration Sep 25, 2026 5:00 PM - 8:30 PM Alvernia University, Francis Hall Theatre Alvernia University’s O’Pake Institute for Economic Development and Entrepreneurship, through its Cultural Coalition, is proud to present Latinos Unidos: A Hispanic Heritage Month Celebration, an inspiring event that honors the rich cultures, traditions, achievements and enduring contributions of Hispanic and Latino communities. Multicultural Engagement Learn more Lead the Pack +1.888.258.3764 400 St. Bernardine Street, Reading, Pa. 19607 admissions@alvernia.edu Main Menu Directory Employment Privacy Policy Accessibility Site Map Alvernia's AI Recruiter Chat with Ashlee © 2026 Alvernia University"
    },
