    "https://www.alvernia.edu/student-experience": {
      "title": "Student Experience",
      "description": "Student Experience | Alvernia University Skip to main content Main navigation Find it About About Who We Are A Franciscan Tradition Rankings & Facts History & Timeline Leadership Mission & Ministry University Information Work at Alvernia Community Engagement CollegeTowne Holleran Center for Community & Global Engagement O'Pake Institute Total Experience Learning Locations Points of Pride Sustainability Culture of Care Network Caring Faculty Ethical Leadership Service Minded Perfectly Located Image News Image Events Image Success Stories Academics Academics Find Your Program Undergraduate Majors Graduate Programs Accelerated Adult Bachelor Programs Online Programs Colleges and Schools Seniors College Experience Learning Apprenticeship to Degree Career Development Experiential Learning O’Pake Fellows SURF Program Holleran Service Opportunities Image Academic Calendar Image Catalog and Handbooks Image Franco Library Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Admission Pathways How to Apply Undergraduate Graduate Adult Education International Corporate Partnerships Military & Veterans Transfer Financial Aid Student Financial Services Tuition & Residential Costs FAFSA: What You Need to Know Scholarships & Awards Visit Campus Graduate, Adult & Continuing Studies Undergraduate Image Apply Now Image Check Application Status Image Request Info Student Experience Student Experience Our Campus Living on Campus Dining Options Our Community Things to Do in the Area Experiences Get Involved Athletics & Recreation Student Organizations and Activities Commuters International Experiences Support SOLAR (Support, Opportunity, Love, Access, Resources) Initiative Academic Support Medical & Counseling Center Community Resources Mission & Ministry Office of Career Development Image Bookstore Image Arts & Culture Image Athletics Resources Resources Information For... Future Students New and First-Year Students Graduate and Adult Students Alumni Parents and Families Community and Partners Find Us Contact Us Faculty/Staff Directory Maps & Directions Image Logins Image Academic Calendar Image Locations FIND IT Visit Apply Now Request Information Virtual Tour Logins Results See All About Directory Student Experience Athletics Maps Jobs at AU Programs Book Store Financial Aid & Tuition Make a Gift Recent News Sep 11, 2026 Alvernia Marks 25th Anniversary of Sept. 11 Through Service and Interfaith Remembrance University launches new Franciscan Fridays service series and gathers faith and community leaders to honor the lives lost and legacy of service  Alvernia University commemorated the 25th anniversary of… Sep 14, 2026 2026 Hispanic Heritage Month at Alvernia Celebrating Hispanic Heritage Month: September 15 to October 15Hispanic Heritage Month is celebrated every September to October. The month allows for individuals to celebrate the histories, cultures, and contributions of… Sep 1, 2026 Alvernia University forms alliance with Independence Blue Cross to Expand Educational Opportunities The new relationship creates flexible, affordable pathways for Independence Blue Cross associates to earn undergraduate and graduate degrees while advancing their careers Alvernia University has joined … See All News Upcoming Events DPT Virtual Information Session Sep 17 Thursday 2026 6:00 PM - 7:00 PM Rhapsody & Song Tickets are $25 and can be purchased online through Eventbrite or at the door.Meet the ArtistsDeanna Reuben, VocalsDeanna Reuben '79 has had an extensive vocal performance… Sep 18 Friday 2026 7:30 PM - 9:30 PM Latinos Unidos: A Hispanic Heritage Month Celebration Register Here Theme: ¡Unidos, Somos Más! (Together, We Are One!)Location: Alvernia University, Francis Hall Atrium and Theatre, 400 Saint Bernardine Street, Reading, PA…, Sep 25 Friday 2026 5:00 PM - 8:30 PM FAQs What type of financial aid is available? At Alvernia, applying for financial aid is easy. We encourage all prospective Alvernia students to apply, even if you feel you may not be eligible for assistance. The Office of Student Financial Services is available to answer questions and guide you through any financial aid situation, email us, call us at 610-796-8201 or stop by the office in Room 114 of Bernardine Hall. Read more financial aid, fees, FAFSA, and billing FAQs How do I Create My Comeback? At Alvernia, we’re in the business of supporting and affirming people in the pursuit of changing their lives for good. If the vision you have of your life includes making an impact on the world, up-leveling your career growth, building a better life for your family, serving your community, or becoming the leader you’ve always known yourself to be - join us to kick-start your next steps. You’re here to get ahead, we're here to help. Contact our knowledgeable admissions coordinators for more information at gradandadult@alvernia.edu , 610-796-5187 When will I receive housing information if I am an incoming first-year or transfer student? The Office of Residence Life will begin to communicate with incoming first-year and transfer students with complete detailed instructions by the end of February.  Our goal is to open the incoming student housing application no later than mid-March. When should I apply? The path to college is a process that typically starts in high school. Our Undergraduate Admissions Office is devoted to helping students and their families through this important and exciting time by arranging visits, hosting events, and answering questions to help you meet future goals and craft a fulfilling life. And, we want you to experience the many ways that Alvernia can help you do this! INQUIRE GIVE VISIT APPLY Breadcrumb Home Student Experience Student Experience Student Experience Alvernia is always in motion. Immersing in a rich campus life, students enjoy a full calendar of activities and events, dozens of organizations, intramural sports, and student leadership and governance opportunities. The Greater Reading region is home to multiple venues offering concerts, shows and sporting events; a thriving food and beverage scene; seasonal festivals; a sprawling community arts center and much more. Attracting a diverse and engaged student body, Alvernia offers a well-rounded experience that is unforgettable. Get Started Request More Info Apply Visit Us Living at Alvernia Residing in Alvernia’s student housing is a popular choice, providing easy access to classrooms, dining halls, fitness facilities and campus activities. Learn More Commuter Resources Many opportunities and resources are offered to benefit commuter students with their educational and social experience. Learn More Student Organizations and Activities Finding new friends, experiences and ways to serve, Alvernia students participate in a wide array of activities. Learn More Global Study Studying abroad is among the most meaningful and edifying opportunities that Alvernia students experience. Learn More Community Service Its roots embedded in Alvernia's foundation, community service provides students the opportunity to use their gifts and talents to help those in need and to support an organization’s purpose-driven mission. Learn More Athletics Competing at the NCAA Division III level, Alvernia's Golden Wolves have made 35 appearances in NCAA Championship tournaments. Learn More Upcoming Events DPT Virtual Information Session Sep 17, 2026 6:00 PM - 7:00 PM Zoom Virtual Event Join us for a virtual information session on September 17, where you’ll learn more about our Doctor of Physical Therapy program. ✔️ Explore the program and curriculum ✔️ Meet our expert faculty ✔️ Get your questions answered about requirements & the application process Whether you’re advancing your education after earning a bachelor’s degree or seeking an accelerated path, Alvernia University’s DPT program offers a comprehensive and compassionate learning experience tailored to your goals. Grad & Adult Admissions Learn more Rhapsody & Song Sep 18, 2026 7:30 PM - 9:30 PM Alvernia University, Francis Hall Theatre An evening of classical, jazz and Broadway music benefiting Alvernia's Hope Fund, which benefits students facing unexpected financial hardships. With special guest vocalist Glynis Fitzgerald, Ph.D., Alvernia University president. Arts & Culture Learn more Latinos Unidos: A Hispanic Heritage Month Celebration Sep 25, 2026 5:00 PM - 8:30 PM Alvernia University, Francis Hall Theatre Alvernia University’s O’Pake Institute for Economic Development and Entrepreneurship, through its Cultural Coalition, is proud to present Latinos Unidos: A Hispanic Heritage Month Celebration, an inspiring event that honors the rich cultures, traditions, achievements and enduring contributions of Hispanic and Latino communities. Multicultural Engagement Learn more Lead the Pack +1.888.258.3764 400 St. Bernardine Street, Reading, Pa. 19607 admissions@alvernia.edu Main Menu Directory Employment Privacy Policy Accessibility Site Map Alvernia's AI Recruiter Chat with Ashlee © 2026 Alvernia University"
    }
